{#- Auto-generated SWAG default (catch-all) vhost config.
    Source: deploy_swag_configs.yaml. Do not edit manually — changes are overwritten
    on next deploy (edit templates/swag_default.conf.j2 instead).

    Handles any request whose Host header doesn't match a known subdomain (the bare
    domain, typos, or internet-wide vulnerability scanners probing IPs directly).

    Root-caused 2026-07-27 (see project_crowdsec_iac.md): this used to rewrite
    unmatched requests to a ~214MB video (a bot tarpit, backed by the now-unused
    `rickroll` container on port 7344) as a deterrent. That worked too well — a
    server-level `rewrite ... last;` here causes nginx to internally redirect to a
    new location BEFORE the CrowdSec access-phase check (`access_by_lua_block`,
    registered globally in the http{} block) has a chance to run for the request,
    so the bounce silently bypassed CrowdSec bans entirely for every request hitting
    this vhost. This isn't a CrowdSec bug — it's an nginx phase-ordering interaction
    specific to a server-level (non-location) `rewrite ... last`. Confirmed via a
    controlled test: the identical banned IP + request was blocked (403) on a normal
    subdomain vhost and bypassed (200, full 214MB) on this one, with debug logging
    showing the CrowdSec access-phase handler never fired in the bypass case.

    Fix: `return 444;` instead of the rewrite. `return` finalizes the request
    immediately wherever it's evaluated, so the outcome (drop the connection, ~0
    bytes) doesn't depend on CrowdSec running at all here — it's unconditional and
    therefore immune to this class of bug by construction, not just a narrower
    version of the same trick. No other site-conf in this repo uses a server-level
    `rewrite ... last`, so this bypass was isolated to this one vhost. -#}
## Managed by homelab-ops (deploy_swag_configs.yaml) — see templates/swag_default.conf.j2

server {
    listen 80 default_server;
    listen [::]:80 default_server;

    location / {
        return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
    }
}

server {
    listen 8081 ssl default_server;
    listen 443 ssl default_server;
    listen [::]:443 ssl default_server;

    server_name _;

    include /config/nginx/ssl.conf;
    include /config/nginx/includes/maxmind.conf;
    include /config/nginx/includes/smdion_errorpages.conf;

    return 444;

    # deny access to .htaccess/.htpasswd files
    location ~ /\.ht {
        deny all;
    }
}
